Y2  - 2022/11/20/
L1  - https://ibethune.github.io/files/cmcgs_bethune.pdf
N1  - <p>Abstract states the project "has discovered over 60 new million-digit primes, as well as record sized twin and Sophie Germain primes" and presents "how the BOINC distributed computing architecture is used to harness tens of thousands of computers." Body describes BOINC client/server architecture, PrimeGrid history (Message@Home renamed PrimeGrid September 2005), subprojects and record primes (Cullen, Woodall, Twin, Sophie Germain, Generalized Fermat, Riesel, AP26), and states "The majority of PrimeGrid's work is done using BOINC." Keywords include "volunteer computing."</p>
