PB  - Springer Berlin Heidelberg
SN  - 978-3-642-55223-6 978-3-642-55224-3
UR  - https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-55224-3_11
Y2  - 2022/11/20/
N1  - <p>Reports Generalized Fermat Number search results from PrimeGrid: "In 2009 PrimeGrid restarted the GFN search beginning from where the previous effort left off" and "Many of these prime searches are coordinated by the PrimeGrid project, which uses the Berkeley Open Infrastructure for Network Computing (BOINC) to allow client computers to download, process, and return work units consisting of primality tests or sieving." Keywords include "Volunteer Computing." Abstract states "The results of the ongoing search are used to extend Gallot and Dubner's published tables... and we report on recent discoveries of GFN primes with over one million digits." References cite the BOINC paper and the PrimeGrid website.</p>
